{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalFourierTransformUnique","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalFourierTransformUnique","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverses.QIntegralTransforms"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalFourier.project_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalFourier.project_const","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-transform-unique.lean#L56-L68","doc":"**Degeneracy of the current `monoidal` law (proved).**\n\nBecause `monoidal` quantifies over *all* convolutions `q_conv`,\nthe projection `project j` is constant in its function argument.\nRecorded as a proved lemma so the structure defect is visible; the\nfix (pin `q_conv` as a field) is the open refactor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalFourier.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalFourier.unique","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-transform-unique.lean#L40-L54","doc":"**Uniqueness of the categorical Fourier transform (proved\nextensionality).**\n\nTwo `CategoricalFourier A Irreps` instances with the same\nprojection family are equal: `monoidal` is propositional.  This\nreplaces a false `Subsingleton (CategoricalFourier A Irreps)`\naxiom with the extensionality the structure genuinely supports. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-fourier-unique","label":"prop:categorical-fourier-unique","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-fourier-transform-unique.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}